{"duration_api_ms":10558,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"f7fe9b64-da62-47c5-9242-b6fd2ef06b9b","total_cost_usd":0.021701800000000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":677,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":807,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":396},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":677,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":807,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":677,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":677},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1243,"outputTokens":27,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.00013780000000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":807,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":677,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.021564000000000003,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":396,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":677,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Written basket policies (Rule 6c-11(c)(3))**\n- The fund must adopt written policies and procedures covering how baskets are built and how they are accepted.\n- If it uses custom baskets, the policies must also:\n  - set detailed parameters for building and accepting them that are in the best interests of the fund and its shareholders;\n  - include a process for revising or deviating from those parameters;\n  - name the titles or roles of the staff who must review each custom basket for compliance.\n\n**Records (Rule 6c-11(d))** must be kept for five years, the first two in an easily accessible place. They include:\n- authorized participant (AP) agreements;\n- for each basket exchanged: the name and quantity of each holding (with ticker, CUSIP or other identifier), any cash amount, whether it was custom, and a statement that it complied with the policies.\n\n**Custom basket versus non-standard order**\n- A **custom basket** depends on composition. It is either not a pro-rata slice of the portfolio, beyond the rule's permitted adjustments, or it differs from other baskets that day.\n- A **non-standard order** is not a term in the rule. It is an operational variation, such as size, cut-off, fees or settlement terms. It is custom only if the basket's composition changes.","ttft_ms":6276,"type":"result","duration_ms":10064,"uuid":"c55efa9a-1342-43bc-8ab1-a3a135464c1a","ttft_stream_ms":1532,"time_to_request_ms":60,"first_content_frame_ms":1532,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
